{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-php-4-1","title":"Philippians 4:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 From particular admonitions, 4 he proceeds to general exhortations, 10 shewing how he rejoiced at their liberality towards him lying in prison, not so much for the supply of his own wants as for the grace of God in them. 19 And so he concludes with prayer and salutations.</p>\n<p>Therefore. 3:20,21; 2Pe 3:11-14 and. 1:8; 2:26 my joy. 2:16; 2Co 1:14; 1Th 2:19,20; 3:9 so. 1:27; Ps 27:14; 125:1; Mt 10:22; Joh 8:31; 15:3,4; Ac 2:42; 11:23 Ac 14:22; Ro 2:7; 1Co 15:58; 16:13; Ga 5:1; Eph 6:10-18; Col 4:12 1Th 3:8,13; 2Th 2:15; 2Ti 2:1; Heb 3:14; 4:14; 10:23,35,36; 2Pe 3:17 Jude 1:20,21,24,25; Re 3:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-4-2","title":"Philippians 4:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>that. 2:2,3; 3:16; Ge 45:24; Ps 133:1-3; Mr 9:50; Ro 12:16-18; 1Co 1:10 Eph 4:1-8; 1Th 5:13; Heb 12:14; Jas 3:17,18; 1Pe 3:8-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-4-3","title":"Philippians 4:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I. 2; Ro 12:1; Phm 1:8,9 true. 2:20-25; Col 1:7 help. 1:27; Ac 9:36-41; 16:14-18; Ro 16:2-4,9,12; 1Ti 5:9,10 whose. Ex 32:32; Ps 69:28; Isa 4:3; Eze 13:9; Da 12:1; Lu 10:20; Re 3:5 Re 13:8; 17:8; 20:12,15; 21:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-4-4","title":"Philippians 4:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Rejoice. 3:1; Ro 12:12 alway. Ps 34:1,2; 145:1,2; 146:2; Mt 5:12; Ac 5:41; 16:25; Ro 5:2,3 1Th 5:16-18; Jas 1:2-4; 1Pe 4:13 again. 3:1; 2Co 13:1,2; Ga 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-4-5","title":"Philippians 4:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":5,"chap